msgid "Adding Hosts at the Second Site"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:241
msgid "Once the cluster is running with NFS storage at the primary site:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:243
msgid ""
"Prepare additional HVM hosts at the second site (see "
":doc:`/getting_started/installation/hvm_host_prep`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:244
msgid "Ensure the NFS endpoint is mountable from the second site hosts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:245
msgid ""
"Add the hosts to the existing cluster: ``Infrastructure > Clusters > "
"[Cluster] > Actions > Add Host``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:246
msgid ""
"|morpheus| will configure the new hosts and mount the NFS datastore "
"automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:248
msgid ""
"Workloads can now be migrated between hosts across sites using Live "
"Migration, provided the NFS storage is accessible from both source and "
"destination hosts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:251
msgid "Multipath NFS Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:253
msgid ""
"For resilient NFS access across sites, configure multipath at the network"
" or NFS appliance level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:255
msgid ""
"**Active/Active NFS endpoints** — If your NFS solution provides multiple "
"access points (e.g., data LIFs across sites), configure DNS round-robin "
"or a load-balanced VIP that routes to the nearest healthy endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:256
msgid ""
"**Active/Passive failover** — If the NFS appliance fails over between "
"sites, ensure the failover IP/VIP is consistent and that hosts reconnect "
"automatically after failover (standard NFS client behavior with ``hard`` "
"mount option)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:257
msgid ""
"**Synchronous replication** — For read/write access from both sites "
"simultaneously, the NFS backend must support synchronous replication. "
"Asynchronous replication introduces the risk of data loss on site "
"failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:259
msgid "Tip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:261
msgid ""
"Use the ``hard`` and ``intr`` NFS mount options in production to ensure "
"clients wait for the NFS server to recover rather than returning errors "
"to applications during brief network interruptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:264
msgid "Failover Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:266
msgid ""
"Unlike the shared LUN model (which uses Corosync/DLM quorum and active "
"fencing), NFS-based stretch clusters rely on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:268
msgid ""
"**NFS appliance failover** — The storage layer handles its own HA. When "
"the NFS endpoint fails over, hosts reconnect and I/O resumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:269
msgid ""
"**|morpheus| host monitoring** — |morpheus| detects host unreachability "
"and can trigger workload migration to surviving hosts (via Dynamic "
"Placement policies)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:270
msgid ""
"**No fencing required** — Since NFS handles locking at the protocol level"
" (NLM/NFSv4 leases), there is no risk of split-brain data corruption that"
" requires active fencing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:272
msgid "If a full site fails:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:274
msgid "|morpheus| detects hosts at the failed site as unreachable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:275
msgid ""
"If Dynamic Placement is enabled with appropriate aggressiveness, "
"workloads are automatically migrated to surviving hosts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:276
msgid ""
"Manual migration can be triggered by placing a host into maintenance mode"
" (``Infrastructure > Servers > [Host] > Actions > Enter Maintenance``). "
"This live-migrates running VMs and moves powered-off VMs to other "
"available hosts in the cluster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:277
msgid ""
"When the failed site recovers, hosts rejoin the cluster and become "
"available for workload placement again"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:280
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:282
msgid ""
"**Performance** — NFS adds network overhead compared to local/Ceph "
"storage. Cross-site NFS access is subject to network latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:283
msgid ""
"**No cluster-level quorum** — The cluster does not independently "
"arbitrate site failures. Failover depends on your NFS appliance's HA "
"capabilities and |morpheus| Dynamic Placement settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:284
msgid ""
"**Write performance across sites** — If hosts at both sites write to the "
"same NFS volume, write performance is bounded by cross-site network "
"latency (especially with synchronous replication)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/stretch_clusters.rst:285
msgid ""
"**Not suitable for all workloads** — Latency-sensitive applications "
"(databases, real-time systems) may not perform well on cross-site NFS. "
"Consider placing these workloads on local storage or site-local NFS "
"exports."
msgstr ""

